      en: "The Bali Bombing Memorial, also known as the Ground Zero Monument, stands in the heart of Kuta at the site of the 2002 terrorist attacks. This carved stone memorial commemorates the 202 people of 22 different nationalities who lost their lives in the tragedy. The design features a large intricate relief and a marble plaque listing the names of all the victims. Every year on October 12th, families, survivors, and officials gather here for a somber ceremony of remembrance. The monument is a powerful symbol of Bali's resilience and the global stand against terrorism, having transformed a place of immense pain into a space for peaceful reflection and international solidarity. Geography K9 — Modern History and Global Security Impacts."
